2025-03-13T22:00:00Z\n## Bug Summary\nThe `should_read_file` method incorrectly 
handles case-insensitive comparison for "full" file reads and fails to find the 
most recent entry for a file when multiple entries exist.\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 1:
The Intent vs. Reality Check** - Logic Gaps\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| 
Expected Behavior | Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| When a file is marked as read 
"full" (case-insensitive), any subsequent read should return False (already 
read) | Only exact lowercase "full" is recognized, "FULL" or "Full" cause the 
method to return True (needs to read) |\n| When multiple entries exist for the 
same file, the most recent entry should be used for comparison | The first 
matching entry is used, which could be outdated |\n| LineRange.from_str("50-10")
should return None for invalid ranges (start > end) | Currently creates a 
LineRange that raises ValueError in __post_init__ |\n\n## Root Cause\n1. **Case 
sensitivity bug**: The code checks `match.lines_read.lower() == "full"` but only
in one place. When `LineRange.from_str()` is called with "FULL" or "Full", it 
returns `None` (invalid format), causing the method to fall through to the 
"invalid lines_read format" path.\n2. **Multiple entries bug**: The code uses 
`next((e for e in reversed(self.recent_files) if e.path == path), None)` which 
correctly iterates in reverse (most recent first), but the test shows it\'s not 
working as expected.\n3. **Invalid range handling**: 
`LineRange.from_str("50-10")` creates a `LineRange(50, 10)` which then raises 
`ValueError` in `__post_init__`. This exception is caught by the try-except, 
returning `None`, but it\'s inefficient and hides the actual error.\n\n## Fix 
Plan\n1. Fix case-insensitive "full" comparison by checking `.lower() == "full"`
before attempting to parse as a range.\n2. Verify the multiple entries logic is 
correct (the code already uses `reversed()`).\n3. Fix `LineRange.from_str()` to 
validate start <= end before creating the object, avoiding the exception.\n4. 
Add comprehensive tests for all edge cases.\n\n## Status: IN PROGRESS'})
